<PageLayout title="Baking Log" subtitle="A printable template for tracking your own bakes.">

  <p>Sourdough rewards keeping notes more than almost anything else in the kitchen — the same recipe behaves differently with a new bag of flour, a warmer kitchen, or a starter that's just hitting its stride. This log gives you a place to put all of that down on paper: dough and ambient temperature, bulk fermentation timing, the poke test, crumb results, and anything you'd want to remember before the next bake.</p>

  <div class="callout printable-extras">
    <strong>Printable:</strong>
    <a href="/downloads/Sourdough_Baking_Log_Template_v10.pdf" class="pdf-pill">Baking Log Template (PDF)</a>
  </div>

  <p>Pair it with the site's <a href="/guides/ph-flour-hydration/">pH, Flour, Hydration, and Temperature</a> and <a href="/guides/proofing-and-shaping/">Proofing and Shaping</a> guides for the small-batch experiments worth logging first — change one variable at a time, write down what actually happened, and your instincts calibrate faster than trial and error alone ever will.</p>

</PageLayout>
